    "description": "Stem Energy Storage Asset SPVs are financing vehicles for behind-the-meter battery storage projects. Their end users are commercial and grid-facing customers that use storage to reduce energy costs, provide local capacity, and support utility programs. The model is asset-heavy and contract-based, with project value tied to financed storage systems and long-term software and services support from Stem. Public reporting identified Generate Capital as a primary Stem project-financing provider in 2016, and Generate's published materials later described a program with the right to fund up to 85 MW / 340 MWh of Southern California behind-the-meter storage projects. The reviewed materials did not disclose individual SPV ownership percentages or portfolio-level revenue. Generate's relationship with Stem therefore centers on project and asset financing, while Stem remains the technology and software provider.",
